  "known_gaps": [
    "Central Logger is SQLite-owned; PostgreSQL event persistence for audit events is delivered via the audit_events/outbox tables in the core PostgreSQL schema, not by migrating the Logger itself.",
    "Raw message bodies are deliberately NOT persisted to logs (minimum-necessary principle); message content is represented by ids, hashes, and type metadata.",
    "Telegram delivery guarantees are Telegram-bound: exactly-once cannot be proven; UNKNOWN is a first-class outcome.",
    "Go worker delivery does not re-evaluate ContentPolicy or apply any task-level transform; the transform package is UNREFERENCED_HELPER (F-08).",
    "Go rulestore never populates FilterRule.BlockLinks (F-12) - latent divergence until Worker activation defaults on.",
    "Emoji removal pattern is byte-identical in Python and Go and destroys non-emoji SMP characters and shreds ZWJ/keycap sequences (F-03).",
    "Header/footer placeholders are not interpolated on the durable pipeline; only the gRPC preview and edit-sync paths expand them (F-15).",
    "The legacy FilterEngine.transform_text orchestrator (services.py:194) is NOT the durable pipeline's transform path; documentation before this audit described the wrong pipeline.",
    "link_policy / domain_allowlist / domain_blocklist / link_rewrite_map are not in SETTING_SPECS, so the validated settings API cannot write them.",
    "filter_inline_keyboard has zero production callers: a link policy strips link text but leaves inline URL buttons (F-16).",
    "dedupe_policy is persisted by SQLite, PostgreSQL, the proto contract and backup/restore, and read by nothing (F-01)."
